T*
(* Back EMF \(E_b\): As the armature rotates, its conductors cut magnetic flux, inducing) Tj
T*
(a counter-EMF opposing supply voltage: E_b = \(P * Phi * Z * N\) / \(60 * A\), where P =) Tj
T*
(poles, Phi = flux/pole, Z = total armature conductors, N = RPM, A = parallel paths \(A) Tj
T*
(= 2 for wave winding, A = P for lap winding\).) Tj
T*
(* Armature Voltage Equation: V = E_b + I_a * R_a.) Tj
T*
(* Armature Torque Equation: Electromagnetic power converted = E_b * I_a = T_e *) Tj
T*
(omega_m = T_e * \(2*pi*N / 60\).) Tj
T*
(T_e = [ \(P * Z\) / \(2 * pi * A\) ] * Phi * I_a = 0.159 * \(P * Z / A\) * Phi * I_a \(Torque) Tj
T*
(is directly proportional to flux and armature current: T_e propto Phi * I_a\).) Tj
