T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Rotating Magnetic Field \(RMF\): Balanced 3-phase currents flowing through spatially) Tj
T*
(displaced stator windings \(120 degrees apart\) produce a magnetic field of constant) Tj
T*
(magnitude \(1.5 * Phi_m\) rotating at Synchronous Speed N_s = 120 * f / P.) Tj
T*
(* Rotor Slip \(s\): Difference between synchronous stator speed and actual rotor speed) Tj
T*
(N_r: s = \(N_s - N_r\) / N_s.) Tj
T*
(* Rotor Current and Torque: Stator RMF cuts stationary rotor bars, inducing rotor) Tj
T*
(currents. Induced currents interact with RMF to produce torque pulling the rotor in) Tj
T*
(the direction of the rotating field. A motor can never run at synchronous speed \(if) Tj
T*
(N_r = N_s, slip = 0, no cutting of flux, torque collapses to zero\).) Tj
T*
