(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A single-phase 2,200 / 220 V, 50 Hz step-down transformer has a net core) Tj
T*
(cross-sectional area of 150 cm^2 \(0.015 m^2\). If the maximum flux density in the core is) Tj
T*
(B_m = 1.2 Tesla, calculate: \(1\) Maximum magnetic flux Phi_m, \(2\) Number of primary turns) Tj
T*
(N1, \(3\) Number of secondary turns N2, \(4\) Primary and secondary full-load currents for a) Tj
T*
(33 kVA rating.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Maximum Core Flux Phi_m:) Tj
T*
(Phi_m = B_m * A = 1.2 T * 0.015 m^2 = 0.018 Webers \(18 mWb\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Number of Primary Turns N1:) Tj
T*
(E1 = 4.44 * f * N1 * Phi_m => N1 = E1 / \(4.44 * f * Phi_m\)) Tj
T*
(N1 = 2200 / \(4.44 * 50 * 0.018\) = 2200 / 3.996 = 550.55 => 551 turns.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Number of Secondary Turns N2:) Tj
T*
(Transformation ratio K = E2 / E1 = 220 / 2200 = 0.10.) Tj
T*
(N2 = K * N1 = 0.10 * 551 = 55.1 => 55 turns.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Compute Full-Load Currents for 33 kVA Rating:) Tj
T*
(Rated Primary Current I1 = Rated kVA * 1000 / V1 = 33,000 / 2200 = 15.0 Amperes.) Tj
T*
(Rated Secondary Current I2 = Rated kVA * 1000 / V2 = 33,000 / 220 = 150.0 Amperes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
