T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A 25 kVA single-phase transformer has a constant core iron loss of 250 W and a) Tj
T*
(full-load copper loss of 400 W. Calculate: \(1\) Efficiency at full load with 0.8 power) Tj
T*
(factor lagging, \(2\) The kVA load at which maximum efficiency occurs, \(3\) Value of) Tj
T*
(maximum efficiency at unity power factor.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Full-Load Efficiency at 0.8 PF Lagging:) Tj
T*
(Output Power = Rated kVA * PF = 25 * 0.8 = 20.0 kW = 20,000 W.) Tj
T*
(Total Losses = Iron Loss + Full-Load Copper Loss = 250 W + 400 W = 650 W.) Tj
T*
(Input Power = Output + Losses = 20,000 + 650 = 20,650 W.) Tj
T*
(Efficiency eta = \(Output / Input\) * 100 = \(20,000 / 20,650\) * 100 = 96.85%.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: kVA Load for Maximum Efficiency:) Tj
T*
(Condition: Variable Copper Loss = Constant Iron Loss.) Tj
T*
(kVA_max = Rated kVA * sqrt\( P_iron / P_cu_FL \) = 25 * sqrt\( 250 / 400 \) = 25 * sqrt\() Tj
T*
(0.625 \)) Tj
T*
(kVA_max = 25 * 0.7906 = 19.76 kVA.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Maximum Efficiency at Unity Power Factor \(PF = 1.0\):) Tj
T*
(Output Power at max efficiency = 19.76 kVA * 1.0 = 19.76 kW = 19,760 W.) Tj
T*
(Total Losses at max efficiency = Iron Loss + Copper Loss = 250 W + 250 W = 500 W.) Tj
T*
(Input Power = 19,760 + 500 = 20,260 W.) Tj
T*
(eta_max = \(19,760 / 20,260\) * 100 = 97.53%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
