([SOLVED PROBLEM 3: DC Shunt Motor Back EMF and Armature Torque]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A 230V DC shunt motor has an armature resistance R_a = 0.5 Omega and field) Tj
T*
(resistance R_sh = 115 Omega. At full load, it draws a total line current of 22A and runs) Tj
T*
(at 1,200 RPM. Calculate: \(1\) Shunt field current I_sh, \(2\) Armature current I_a, \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Back EMF E_b, \(4\) Developed electromagnetic torque T_e.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate Field Current I_sh:) Tj
T*
(I_sh = V / R_sh = 230 V / 115 Omega = 2.0 Amperes.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Armature Current I_a:) Tj
T*
(I_a = I_line - I_sh = 22.0 A - 2.0 A = 20.0 Amperes.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Back EMF E_b:) Tj
T*
(E_b = V - I_a * R_a = 230 - \(20.0 * 0.5\) = 230 - 10.0 = 220.0 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Compute Electromagnetic Torque T_e:) Tj
T*
(Mechanical Power converted P_mech = E_b * I_a = 220 V * 20 A = 4,400 Watts.) Tj
T*
(Angular Velocity omega_m = 2 * pi * N / 60 = 2 * pi * 1200 / 60 = 40 * pi = 125.66) Tj
T*
(rad/sec.) Tj
T*
(Torque T_e = P_mech / omega_m = 4400 / 125.66 = 35.01 N*m \(Newton-meters\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
