(Problem: A 4-pole, 50 Hz, 3-phase induction motor runs at a rotor speed of 1,440 RPM at) Tj
T*
(full load. Calculate: \(1\) Synchronous speed N_s, \(2\) Slip s, \(3\) Percentage slip %s, \(4\)) Tj
T*
(Frequency of rotor induced currents f_r.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Synchronous Speed N_s:) Tj
T*
(N_s = 120 * f / P = \(120 * 50\) / 4 = 6,000 / 4 = 1,500 RPM.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Fractional Slip s:) Tj
T*
(s = \(N_s - N_r\) / N_s = \(1500 - 1440\) / 1500 = 60 / 1500 = 0.04 \(4.0%\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Rotor Current Frequency f_r:) Tj
T*
(f_r = s * f = 0.04 * 50 Hz = 2.0 Hz.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Under operating conditions, rotor currents oscillate at only 2 Hz,) Tj
T*
(minimizing rotor iron core losses.) Tj
T*
