(>> 3.5 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Derive the condition for maximum efficiency of a transformer from first) Tj
T*
(principles.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Let transformer rating be S \(VA\), output power P_out = V2 * I2 * cos\(phi\). Total) Tj
T*
(losses are Iron Loss \(P_i, constant\) and Copper Loss \(P_cu = I2^2 * R_02, variable\).) Tj
T*
(Efficiency is eta = P_out / \(P_out + Losses\) = [ V2 * I2 * cos\(phi\) ] / [ V2 * I2 *) Tj
T*
(cos\(phi\) + P_i + I2^2 * R_02 ]. Divide numerator and denominator by I2: eta = [ V2 *) Tj
T*
(cos\(phi\) ] / [ V2 * cos\(phi\) + P_i / I2 + I2 * R_02 ]. For maximum efficiency with) Tj
T*
(respect to load current I2, the denominator must be minimized. Differentiating) Tj
T*
(denominator with respect to I2 and setting to zero: d/dI2 [ V2*cos\(phi\) + P_i / I2 + I2) Tj
T*
(* R_02 ] = - P_i / \(I2\)^2 + R_02 = 0 => P_i = \(I2\)^2 * R_02 = P_cu. Therefore, maximum) Tj
T*
(efficiency occurs when variable copper loss equals constant core iron loss.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain why a 3-phase induction motor is self-starting whereas a single-phase) Tj
T*
(induction motor is not.) Tj
T*
(Answer: When 3-phase balanced currents flow through 3-phase stator windings spaced 120) Tj
T*
(degrees apart, they produce a true Rotating Magnetic Field \(RMF\) of constant magnitude) Tj
T*
(1.5*Phi_m that rotates at synchronous speed N_s. This RMF cuts stationary rotor) Tj
T*
(conductors, inducing currents that create a unidirectional starting torque. In contrast,) Tj
T*
(a single-phase stator winding produces a pulsating stationary magnetic field that) Tj
T*
(alternates along a single spatial axis without rotation. By Double Revolving Field) Tj
T*
(Theory, a pulsating field decomposes into two equal fields rotating in OPPOSITE) Tj
T*
(directions at speed N_s. At standstill \(N = 0\), both fields exert equal and opposite) Tj
T*
(torques; net starting torque is identically zero. Hence, single-phase motors require) Tj
T*
(auxiliary starting windings or split-phase capacitors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
